<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30703" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑδραῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Pl.
			<u>R.</u>
			407b
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Plu.
			2.288d
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sitting,
				sedentary</i>, of persons or their occupations, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔργον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					53
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ πολλοὶ τῶν τὰς τέχνας ἐχόντων
					ἑδραῖοί εἰσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Lac.</u>
					1.3
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. ἀρχαί</span>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατεῖαι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				407b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.42
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Crin.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑδραία ῥάχις</span> the horse's back
				<i>on which the rider sits</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				783
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>steady, steadfast</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάθησ᾽ ἑδραία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					266
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῖ τὴν γυναῖκα ὥσπερ κύβον ἑδραῖον
					εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.288d
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				952d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύβος -ότατον σῶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ti.Locr.
					98c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. βάσεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ti.</u>
					59d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑδραιότατον στοιχεῖον εἶναι τὴν γῆν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Heraclit.
					<u>All.</u>
					41
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὂν τὸ πάντων -ότατον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plot.
					6.2.8
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. ὕπνος</span>
			<i>sound</i> sleep, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				6.4.15
			</span></i>; of a cup, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				11.496a
			</span></i>: metaph. in Rhet., <i>firmly based</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατάληξις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Demetr.
					<u>Eloc.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Longin.
				40.4
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αίως</span>
			<i>firmly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.Mech.
				36.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				3.14.5
			</span></i>; <i>steadily</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>Hyp.</u>
				3.21
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>permanently appointed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PStrassb.
				40.11
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(vi A. D.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
